# `format`/`format:check` in the root package.json pass BOTH ignore files:
#     --ignore-path ../../.gitignore --ignore-path ../../.prettierignore
# and the first of those two flags is not decoration. An explicit --ignore-path REPLACES Prettier
# 3's default of [".gitignore", ".prettierignore"] rather than adding to it, so the single-flag form
# silently drops .gitignore and the check walks node_modules, .venv, vendor, every tool cache and
# the pnpm store — measured at 4,855 unformatted files, of which 4,697 were machine-written.
# Naming both files is the structural fix; mirroring .gitignore into this file forever is a standing
# drift obligation that gets forgotten exactly once and then silently.
#
# A handful of gitignored paths are ALSO listed below on purpose. They are redundant while the
# flag above is correct, and they are three lines of insurance against the day it is not.

# Lockfiles: reformatting one changes bytes CI hashes for its cache key and its osv-scanner run.
pnpm-lock.yaml
composer.lock
uv.lock
requirements.lock

# Build and tool output.
node_modules/
dist/
.next/
out/
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
vendor/
.venv/

# Tool caches. Machine-written JSON regenerated on every run; services/ai-service/.mypy_cache alone
# holds ~3,175 stub files, which is 65% of everything the repo-root check walks.
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Regenerated by `next build`/`next dev` and carrying its own "This file should not be edited"
# header — so formatting it is undone by the next build, and whether the check passes depends on
# whether anyone has built. It appeared in this list the first time `pnpm web:build` was run.
apps/web/next-env.d.ts

# pnpm's content-addressable store. It lands at the REPO ROOT whenever HOME is redirected into the
# tree — which is what a containerized `pnpm install` does — and is 882 MB-1.3 GB of package
# tarballs and JSON index files. Measured: 1,522 of them are .json and Prettier reads every one.
.pnpm-store/

# Committed generator output. `pnpm tokens:build && git diff --exit-code` is the CI gate; a
# formatter rewriting these files fails that diff against a generator that is behaving correctly.
packages/design-tokens/generated/
packages/contracts/rules/
packages/contracts/openapi/

# The specification is extracted verbatim from KnowledgeBot-AI.md; reflowing it destroys the diff
# against the source document.
KnowledgeBot-AI.md
docs/

# The agent and skill library. These are contracts an agent reads verbatim, not source: reflowing a
# table, a fenced block, or a `<!-- UNVERIFIED -->` comment changes the instruction, and docs/ cites
# them by line. 88 of them are unformatted today and none of them should be touched by a formatter.
.claude/

# Trees whose formatter is not Prettier and whose owner is not the Node tier. Prettier here is a
# devDependency of apps/web, so a repo-root run makes ONE app's Prettier version the arbiter of
# every other owner's bytes; each line below names the toolchain that already owns those files.
#
# PHP + Python. Pint formats the Laravel side and Ruff the FastAPI side; composer.json is rewritten
# by Composer itself on every `composer require`, so a Prettier pass over it is a standing diff.
services/
# Compose, Traefik, Prometheus, Loki, Tempo and Alertmanager configuration, owned by
# platform-devops-engineer. Prettier's YAML printer re-quotes and re-indents in ways those parsers
# accept but an ops reviewer should not have to read past in a diff.
infrastructure/
# The golden eval corpus. BYTE-STABLE BY CONSTRUCTION, not by convention: rag-eval-engineer records
# a sha256 of every fixture in the corpus manifest, and the eval regression gate measures against
# those hashes — so a whitespace-only Prettier pass invalidates the entire baseline. Written only by
# rag-eval-engineer (CLAUDE.md); read-only for everyone else, including formatters.
samples/
# Repo-level developer and operational scripts — written only by platform-devops-engineer.
scripts/
